## Troubleshooting

### "Permission denied for schema public"

The runtime role needs `USAGE` on `public`. If you revoke and recreate the role, re-run the GRANT statements from the init SQL.

### "Must be superuser to alter default privileges"

`ALTER DEFAULT PRIVILEGES` must be run as the role that will own future tables (typically the superuser). The init SQL handles this automatically in Docker Compose; for manual deploys, run it as the superuser.

### Migrations fail with "permission denied"

Ensure you are running migrations with `DATABASE_URL` (superuser), not `RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL`. The generated `start.sh` handles this automatically with the one-shot `QUICKSCALE_PRIVILEGED_COMMAND=migrate` inline prefix. If you run migrations manually:

```bash
# Override the runtime URL to use the superuser connection
# (one-shot inline prefix — never persistent configuration)
QUICKSCALE_PRIVILEGED_COMMAND=migrate RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL="" python manage.py migrate --noinput
```
